      "subject": "Runtime tests never write to runtime-data, and test:runtime enforces it",
      "body": "In PRODUCTION_ADMISSION the replay orchestrator saved the correlation\nthrough a store built with no root, so it rewrote two fixture\ncorrelations in the real runtime-data on every test run, even when the\ntest injected temporary replay storage. The orchestrator now takes the\ncorrelation store from its input, and a test that configures no root\ngets the F-25 isolated temporary root. All 1,580 Runtime tests were\nchecked: this was the only write outside temporary roots.\n\nnpm run test:runtime runs every Runtime test and fails if runtime-data\nor runtime/ changed during the run, by size and mtime, so a rewrite of\nan existing file is caught too.\n\nMission: MS-2026-0008\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
